    classification: "TENANT_RLS_REQUIRED",
    reason: "PROVEN (2026-09-04, finance.ts round 32, CORRECTED same round after independent review found a load-bearing lifecycle defect in the first pass — see the correction note at the end of this reason): closes the isolation gap round 31 correctly reopened this to NEEDS_REVIEW for. Django execution-principal facts (Phase 1/2; see apps/union-eyes/backend/billing/isolation.py's module docstring for the full evidence chain): per .github/workflows/deploy-union-eyes.yml's backend deploy step, Django's PGUSER/PGPASSWORD are DERIVED FROM the frontend container's `union-eyes-runtime-database-url`-backed DATABASE_URL secret — i.e. Django is INTENDED, by deployment wiring, to connect as the same `union_eyes_runtime` role (NOSUPERUSER/NOBYPASSRLS per scripts/provision-runtime-db-roles.ts) Next.js uses for its tenant-scoped client. BLOCKED_EXTERNAL_ACCESS: the actual live-deployed credential/role was NOT independently queried in this round (no read-only DB access available in this environment) — this is the intended principal proven from deployment wiring, not an empirically attested live value. This table has no Postgres RLS policy today regardless (only the 24 baseline-0108.ts tables do), so isolation is enforced entirely at the Django application layer. `ChartOfAccountsViewSet` applies `DirectTenantIsolationMixin` (apps/union-eyes/backend/billing/isolation.py), which: (1) filters get_queryset() to `organization_id = request.organization_id`; (2) forces organization_id to the caller's own org on create, discarding any client-supplied value; (3) re-verifies the row's organization_id against the caller's before allowing update/delete, and forces it back on every update so a caller cannot reassign the row to another organization; (4) fails closed (empty queryset / rejected mutation) if request.organization_id is absent. CORRECTION (same round, independent review): request.organization_id was ORIGINALLY documented as set by auth_core.middleware.OrganizationIsolationMiddleware from the verified JWT organization claim. That was wrong in a load-bearing way — OrganizationIsolationMiddleware is Django middleware (config/settings.py MIDDLEWARE), which runs BEFORE the view, and therefore BEFORE DRF's authentication classes ever execute (DRF auth happens inside APIView.dispatch(), after the whole Django middleware chain has completed) — auth_core.authentication.OIDCAuthentication.authenticate() is the ONLY thing that ever set the request.org_id attribute the middleware read, so for every real bearer-token request the middleware always saw org_id as absent and request.organization_id was NEVER populated. All 20 of this round's ViewSets were therefore fail-closed for ALL real traffic (safe, but not functioning tenant-scoped endpoints) until this correction. FIXED by moving organization resolution into a new auth_core.authentication.resolve_organization_context() function, called directly from OIDCAuthentication.authenticate() immediately after the org claim is verified — the only point in the lifecycle guaranteed to run before any view/queryset code; OrganizationIsolationMiddleware now only sets safe defaults and no longer attempts resolution. Read+write isolation proof now spans two levels: (a) mixin-logic unit tests in apps/union-eyes/backend/billing/tests_isolation.py (mocked queryset/serializer, proves the filter/force/reject decisions), and (b) REAL request-lifecycle integration tests in apps/union-eyes/backend/billing/tests_request_lifecycle.py, which call the actual OIDCAuthentication.authenticate() (mocking only the JWKS network call and the Organizations DB query — no reachable Postgres/JWKS server in this sandbox) and then run the real mixin against the SAME request object authenticate() populated, never test-injecting request.organization_id directly — including a negative fixture proving the mixin alone, without this propagation, stays fail-closed rather than silently working. Run via `python -m unittest billing.tests_isolation billing.tests_request_lifecycle` (16 + 7 tests, all pass). Direct NOT NULL-in-practice organization_id column confirmed in billing/models.py.",
